@startuml
title Book and pay from the web or mobile client | FR-007, FR-009 | Current implementation
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
skinparam activityBorderColor #475569
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #475569
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
skinparam stateBorderColor #475569
actor Learner as L
participant "Web or mobile booking screen" as UI
participant "Gateway" as G
participant "Live Class" as LC
participant "Wallet Ledger" as WL
L -> UI: Open a published class
UI -> G: GET /api/classes/:id
G -> LC: Read the class and its free seats
LC --> G: Class detail
G --> UI: Class detail
L -> UI: Choose Book class
UI -> G: POST /api/classes/:id/bookings
G -> LC: Hold a seat (row-locked, idempotent by key)
alt Booking refused
 LC --> G: Reason (insufficient balance, full, too late, duplicate)
 G --> UI: Reason
 UI --> L: Show the reason; nothing was booked
else Booking held
 LC --> G: Booking id + price, status Pending
 G --> UI: Booking id + price
 UI -> G: POST /api/classes/bookings/:bookingId/confirm
 G -> LC: Commit the booking and emit booking.confirmed
 LC -> WL: Settle the escrow (asynchronous, idempotent consumer)
 UI --> L: Confirmation; the seat is really reserved
end
note over UI,WL: Both clients post to the real hold and confirm endpoints.\nConfirmation is committed before wallet settlement, so settlement\nis asynchronous and the client must not assume it has happened.\nMock gateways remain only as an unconfigured-build fallback on mobile.
@enduml
